# ======================================================================
# VALO Tech — .gitignore
#
# Organised by blast radius: what must never leak comes first, what
# merely clutters comes last.
#
#   1. Secrets, credentials, key material
#   2. Environment files
#   3. Node tooling
#   4. IDE / editor / OS residue
#   5. Agent + session scratch
#
# This repository IS the deployed artifact — GitHub Pages serves the
# tree verbatim at valotech.org. Ignoring a served file removes it from
# the site, so no rule here may ever match an asset, page, or config
# the site loads. There is no build step and nothing to regenerate.
#
# Conventions:
#   · Entries are alphabetised within each section.
#   · A negation (`!`) must follow a pattern that excludes directory
#     ENTRIES (`dir/*`), never the directory itself (`dir/`) — git
#     cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
#   · A blanket extension rule (`*.key`) is paired with an explicit
#     directory rule (`keys/`), so relocating a file cannot bypass it.
# ======================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets, credentials, key material — never commit, no exceptions
#    Pure insurance: this site uses none. But the repo publishes to a
#    public host on every push, so a committed key is public instantly.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cer
*.crt
*.jks
*.key
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
*.pfx
credentials.json
keys/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Environment files
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.envrc

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Node tooling — the ecosystem raster pipeline (sharp, png-to-ico) is
#    run ad hoc; its install must never land in the published tree.
#    Debug logs need no rule here: section 4's `*.log` already covers
#    them. A lockfile deliberately has no rule — if this repo ever gains
#    a real Node project, its lockfile must be committed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. IDE / editor / OS residue
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.log
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.swo
*.swp
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Agent + session scratch
#    Claude Code state is per-machine and regenerated; only the shared,
#    reviewed configuration below is committed. An allowlist cannot be
#    outrun by a new runtime directory the way a blocklist can. The
#    reviewed hand-authored skills under .claude/skills/ are committed as
#    shared, reviewed configuration; a regenerated or vendored skills
#    tree (the kind removed in c77ae08) stays out as runtime state.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.playwright-mcp/
